{"event":"intent","sources":["origin","f001","f005"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s02; BRANCH=gro-frag-stale-ptr; Search only snapshots/s02 and never open any other snapshot. GRO/segmentation/frag-list lifetime analogue of the seed's use-after-free: *_gro_receive and *_gro_complete handlers, GSO segmenters, and frag-list walkers that capture pointers into per-packet headers — skb_gro_header_pointer()/skb_gro_header_slow() results, gro network-header pointers, pointers into frag-list data or skb_shinfo — hold them across skb_gro_pull(), pskb_may_pull() over frag lists, skb_gro_receive(), or other head-relocation/frag-consumption, and then dereference the stale pointer without re-fetching via skb_gro_header_fast()/skb_gro_header_slow(); pskb_expand_head()/head relocation frees the old head, so pre-relocation pointer reuse is exactly the seed's bug class. The tx-cow-head-realloc pass on this snapshot already covered batman-adv and mac80211 linearize/cow call sites — do not re-audit those; focus strictly on GRO/GSO/frag-list paths (net/core gro core, per-protocol *_gro_receive/*_gro_complete, drivers/ gro callbacks). Record exact file:function:line evidence (pointer capture, relocating call, every stale dereference) per candidate or an evidence-backed negative of what was searched. Save a structured artifact for snapshot s02 only."}
{"event":"intent","sources":["origin","f001","f002"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s03; BRANCH=gro-frag-stale-ptr; Search only snapshots/s03 and never open any other snapshot. Cross-subsystem GRO/segmentation/frag-list analogue: *_gro_receive/*_gro_complete handlers, GSO segmenters, and frag-list walkers that hold pointers into per-packet headers — skb_gro_header_pointer()/skb_gro_header_slow() results, gro network-header pointers, pointers into frag-list data or skb_shinfo — across skb_gro_pull(), pskb_may_pull() over frag lists, skb_gro_receive(), or other head-relocation/frag-consumption, and dereference them afterwards without re-fetching via skb_gro_header_fast()/skb_gro_header_slow(). Any pointer captured before a head-relocating or frag-consuming call and used after it is the seed's pep_get_sb() use-after-free class. The tx-cow-head-realloc pass on this snapshot already covered mac80211 and mt76 linearize sites — restrict to GRO/GSO/frag-list code paths, including drivers/ gro callbacks. Record exact file:function:line evidence (capture, relocating call, stale use) per candidate or an evidence-backed negative of what was searched. Save a structured artifact for snapshot s03 only."}
{"event":"intent","sources":["origin","f001","f003"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s04; BRANCH=gro-frag-stale-ptr; Search only snapshots/s04 and never open any other snapshot. GRO/segmentation/frag-list stale-pointer analogue of the seed's use-after-free: *_gro_receive/*_gro_complete handlers, GSO segmenters, and frag-list walkers that capture per-packet header pointers — skb_gro_header_pointer()/skb_gro_header_slow() results, gro network-header pointers, pointers into frag-list data or skb_shinfo — keep them live across skb_gro_pull(), pskb_may_pull() over frag lists, skb_gro_receive(), or other head-relocation/frag-consumption, and dereference them afterwards without re-fetching; head relocation frees the old buffer, making every pre-relocation pointer a potential slab use-after-free exactly like ph in pep_get_sb(). The loop-parser-stale-state pass on this snapshot already covered GARP/X25/batman-adv/NFC parse loops — restrict to GRO/GSO/frag-list paths, including drivers/ gro callbacks. Record exact file:function:line evidence (pointer capture, relocating call, every stale dereference) per candidate or an evidence-backed negative of what was searched. Save a structured artifact for snapshot s04 only."}
{"event":"intent","sources":["origin","f001","f004"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s05; BRANCH=gro-frag-stale-ptr; Search only snapshots/s05 and never open any other snapshot. GRO/segmentation/frag-list analogue: *_gro_receive/*_gro_complete handlers, GSO segmenters, and frag-list walkers that hold pointers into per-packet headers — skb_gro_header_pointer()/skb_gro_header_slow() results, gro network-header pointers, pointers into frag-list data or skb_shinfo — across skb_gro_pull(), pskb_may_pull() over frag lists, skb_gro_receive(), or other head-relocation/frag-consumption, and dereference them afterwards without re-fetching via skb_gro_header_fast()/skb_gro_header_slow(). Any pointer captured before a head-relocating or frag-consuming call and dereferenced after is the seed's use-after-free class on a different subsystem surface. The loop-parser-stale-state pass on this snapshot already covered MPLS/X25/IPv6/IPVS parse loops — restrict to GRO/GSO/frag-list code paths, including drivers/ gro callbacks. Record exact file:function:line evidence (capture, relocating call, stale use) per candidate or an evidence-backed negative of what was searched. Save a structured artifact for snapshot s05 only."}
